<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  MatchDay's app-level privacy manifest.

  ── WHY EVERY ARRAY IS EMPTY, AND WHY THAT IS AUDITED ──────────────────────

  Re-verified for Build #2, which adds @capacitor/push-notifications to the
  set — @capacitor/core, /ios, /app, /browser, /push-notifications,
  /splash-screen and /status-bar — by scanning all 118 Swift and Objective-C
  sources (113 excluding the packages' own test targets) for each of Apple's
  five required-reason API categories:

      UserDefaults .............. 0 uses
      file timestamp ............ 0 uses
      system boot time .......... 0 uses
      disk space ................ 0 uses
      active keyboard ........... 0 uses

  The one nearby hit, `.fileSizeKey` in Capacitor's WebViewAssetHandler, reads
  the size of a specific bundled file. That is not the disk-space category and
  needs no declaration.

  ── NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes IS EMPTY ON PURPOSE ────────────────────────

  This manifest describes what the *native layer* collects, and it collects
  nothing: the shell renders a webview and nothing else. What MatchDay collects
  as a product — name, email, league participation and the rest — is declared in
  App Store Connect's App Privacy questionnaire and documented at /privacy.
  Duplicating it here would create a second inventory to keep in sync.

  ── TRACKING IS FALSE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  No advertising SDK, no attribution, no IDFA, no cross-app linkage, and no
  ATT prompt. Build #2 adds an APNs device token, which is an identifier used
  for app functionality — it is not tracking and does not change this file.

  ── THIS FILE HAS TO BE IN THE TARGET TO COUNT ─────────────────────────────

  It exists in the repository from Build #1 but was never a member of the App
  target, so it was not copied into the bundle and Apple never saw it. A
  manifest that is not in the built product is indistinguishable from no
  manifest at all, and the omission is silent in both directions: the build
  succeeds and the upload is accepted. It is a resource of the App target as of
  Build #2 — see PBXResourcesBuildPhase in project.pbxproj.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
